fails when Meta.ordering contains expressions (OrderBy/F) during multi-table inheritance ordering resolution. Need to support expressions when resolving related model ordering in compiler.find_ordering_name to avoid passing expressions to get_order_dir (which expects a string).\"},{\"id\":\"phase2\",\"title\":\"Run the test suite to observe failing tests related to the issue\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},{\"id\":\"phase3\",\"title\":\"Explore codebase to find relevant functions/classes and files (e.g., get_order_dir)\",\"status\":\"done\",\"notes\":\"Found get_order_dir in django/db/models/sql/query.py and its use in django/db/models/sql/compiler.py. The bug arises when Meta.ordering contains expressions and compiler.find_ordering_name iterates opts.ordering and passes items to get_order_dir expecting strings. Implemented support for expressions at start of find_ordering_name.\"},{\"id\":\"phase4\",\"title\":\"Create a minimal reproduction script to confirm the issue if tests are heavy\",\"status\":\"todo\"},{\"id\":\"phase5\",\"title\":\"Analyze and decide the minimal fix approach\",\"status\":\"done\",\"notes\":\"Minimal fix: Handle expression items in find_ordering_name by converting to OrderBy and respecting default_order, mirroring logic from get_order_by.\"},{\"id\":\"phase6\",\"title\":\"Implement the fix in source files\",\"status\":\"done\",\"notes\":\"Edited django/db/models/sql/compiler.py to support expressions in find_ordering_name.\"},{\"id\":\"phase7\",\"title\":\"Verify with tests and reproduction script\",\"status\":\"todo\"},{\"id\":\"phase8\",\"title\":\"Final review against requirements and base commit\",\"status\":\"todo\"}]}"}}]}, {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Task list has been updated with 8 items. Stored in session directory: sessions/817beb01-a92d-40-6d4ef6c470d8f13/TASKS.md"}], "role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_rgR0LYGmqvCXvdwVFhK6FwSe", "name": "task_tracker"}, {"content": [], "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_